#! ia 1.0

@category thing
  meaning
    says "A concrete entity — an object or instance that exists in its own right."
    answers "Is this node a concrete instance that exists in its own right, not a type of one?"
  data
    order 0

@category kind
  meaning
    says "A type or class — the category an instance belongs to."
    answers "Is this node a type that instances belong to, not one of those instances?"
  data
    order 1

@category property
  meaning
    says "An attribute or quality — a characteristic a node carries."
    answers "Is this node a characteristic that some other node carries?"
  data
    order 2

@category state
  meaning
    says "A condition or status — the configuration a node is in at a moment."
    answers "Is this node the condition something is in at a moment, not what happened to it?"
  data
    order 3

@category event
  meaning
    says "An occurrence in time — something that happens or is emitted."
    answers "Is this node something that happens or is emitted at a point in time?"
  data
    order 4

@category relation
  meaning
    says "A link between nodes — an edge or association connecting two things."
    answers "Is this node an association that connects two other things?"
  data
    order 5

@category rule
  meaning
    says "A normative constraint — what must, may, or must not hold."
    answers "Is this node a statement of what must, may or must not hold?"
  data
    order 6

@category capability
  meaning
    says "An ability or affordance — what an actor or system can do."
    answers "Is this node something an actor or system is able to do?"
  data
    order 7

@category intent
  meaning
    says "A goal or purpose — the aim a node is directed toward."
    answers "Is this node an aim that work is directed toward?"
  data
    order 8

@category decision
  meaning
    says "A committed choice — a selection among alternatives, with the bet stated."
    answers "Is this node a choice already committed among alternatives, with its bet stated?"
  data
    order 9

@category evidence
  meaning
    says "A grounding observation — a checkable fact that supports a claim."
    answers "Is this node a checkable fact offered in support of a claim?"
  data
    order 10

@category representation
  meaning
    says "A data shape or encoding — how information is structured or rendered."
    answers "Is this node a structure or encoding for information, not the information's subject?"
  data
    order 11

@category process
  meaning
    says "An activity or transformation — work that takes inputs to outputs over steps."
    answers "Is this node work that turns inputs into outputs over steps?"
  data
    order 12

@category measure
  meaning
    says "A quantity or metric — a measured value or unit of assessment."
    answers "Is this node a quantity, or a unit for assessing one?"
  data
    order 13

@category boundary
  meaning
    says "A scope or limit — the edge of a domain, where reach or authority stops."
    answers "Is this node where scope or authority stops, rather than a rule about it?"
  data
    order 14

